\subsection{Twelve High-Priority Golden Rules to Memorize}

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{AES Block Invariant:} AES block size is \textbf{always 128 bits}, regardless of key length ($128, 192$, or $256$ bits).
\item \textbf{MixColumns Invariant:} MixColumns is applied in all AES rounds \textbf{except the final round}.
\item \textbf{DES Key Space:} DES effective key length is \textbf{56 bits} ($8$ parity bits discarded from $64$ nominal bits); broken by brute force.
\item \textbf{3DES Deprecation:} 3DES uses Encrypt-Decrypt-Encrypt (EDE); disallowed by NIST after December 31, 2023 due to 64-bit Sweet32 collision attacks.
\item \textbf{RSA Modulus and Totient:} $n = p \cdot q$ and $\phi(n) = (p-1)(q-1)$; public exponent $e$ must satisfy $\gcd(e, \phi(n)) = 1$; private exponent $d \equiv e^{-1} \pmod{\phi(n)}$.
\item \textbf{Hybrid Encryption Rule:} Asymmetric encryption protects the small symmetric session key; symmetric encryption protects bulk data.
\item \textbf{SAST vs. DAST Rule:} SAST tests code without execution (white-box); DAST tests a running application externally (black-box).
\item \textbf{PIN Search Space:} 4-digit PIN $= 10^4 = 10,000$ combinations; 6-digit PIN $= 10^6 = 1,000,000$ combinations; mandates lockout after 3--5 failed attempts.
\item \textbf{Zero Plaintext PIN Storage:} Plaintext PINs must \textbf{never} be logged, written to disk, or kept in memory; must use HSMs or slow salted hashes.
\item \textbf{Class Imbalance Fallacy:} In intrusion detection, accuracy is meaningless ($99.99\%$ accuracy can have $0\%$ attack detection recall); prioritize Recall, Precision, and F1-Score.
\item \textbf{Adversarial Lifecycle Timing:} Data Poisoning attacks the \textbf{training phase}; Evasion attacks the \textbf{inference phase}.
\item \textbf{GenAI Security Principle:} Always enforce separation of instruction and data planes; AI agents must operate under least privilege with Human-in-the-Loop for destructive actions.
\end{enumerate}

